From 26d5ed7fcc2bcb47fea14b569dc87f43a2373495 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lesssalt <lesssalt@proton.me>
Date: Fri, 6 Dec 2024 23:23:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add link hint functionality

This patch provides link hint functionality requested in Github issue
#188 by introducing several commands. It uses the existing
getLinkNumberStr function and adds the option to display and input link
numbers using alpha characters, with the new displayLinkAlpha option.
Updates manual and README.func.

When a command is called:
* link numbers are displayed if not already
* w3m prompts the user to input the number of the target link
* the user inputs the link number or cancels input
* if a valid link number, the program will act on that hyperlink
* if an invalid link number, the program will display error message
* after action, link numbers are toggled off if not on previously

Commands:
* MOVE_LINK_NUM moves the cursor to the position of the hyperlink
* GOTO_LINK_NUM follows the hyperlink
* TAB_LINK_NUM follows link in tab; the tab number can be prefixed
* MENU_LINK_NUM opens default menu or a named menu on top of the link

These commands temporarily disable marked urls while displaying link
numbers to avoid confusion seen in Github issues #180 and #298.
Add commands to the manual and update README.func

Example keymap configuration:
```
keymap  f GOTO_LINK_NUM
keymap  F TAB_LINK_NUM
keymap  m MOVE_LINK_NUM
keymap  M MENU_LINK_NUM
```
